flowchart TB
    accTitle: CoALA memory landscape
    accDescr: Working memory is the short-term active store for the current decision cycle. Long-term memory is divided into episodic, semantic, and procedural categories.

    subgraph shortterm["Short-term memory"]
      WM["Working memory<br/>Active information for the current decision cycle"]
    end

    subgraph longterm["Long-term memory"]
      EPI["Episodic memory<br/>Experience from earlier cycles"]
      SEM["Semantic memory<br/>Knowledge about the world and the agent"]
      PROC["Procedural memory<br/>Implicit model knowledge and explicit agent code"]
    end

    classDef active fill:#EAF4FB,stroke:#1A4A8A,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:2px;
    classDef retained fill:#EEF7EE,stroke:#27AE60,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.5px;
    class WM active;
    class EPI,SEM,PROC retained;
